### Production Implementation Strategies

Implementing ElevenLabs Studio 3.0 in production environments requires careful consideration of performance, cost optimization, and quality consistency:

\`\`\`typescript
// Production-ready ElevenLabs integration with optimization
export class ProductionAudioSystem {
  private studioIntegration: ElevenLabsStudioIntegration
  private audioCache: AudioCacheManager
  private qualityMonitor: AudioQualityMonitor
  private costOptimizer: CostOptimizationEngine

  constructor() {
    this.setupProductionInfrastructure()
  }

  // Intelligent caching system for audio content
  private setupAudioCaching(): void {
    this.audioCache = new AudioCacheManager({
      storage: 'redis', // Use Redis for fast audio retrieval
      maxSize: '10GB',
      ttl: 7 * 24 * 60 * 60, // 7 days
      compression: 'opus', // Optimal compression for voice
      qualityLevels: ['low', 'medium', 'high', 'studio'],
      smartEviction: true
    })
  }

  // Cost optimization through intelligent request batching
  async optimizeAudioGeneration(requests: AudioRequest[]): Promise<AudioResponse[]> {
    // Group similar requests for batch processing
    const batchGroups = this.groupSimilarRequests(requests)

    const results = await Promise.all(
      batchGroups.map(async (group) => {
        const cacheKey = this.generateCacheKey(group.config)
        const cached = await this.audioCache.get(cacheKey)

        if (cached) {
          return this.applyCachedAudio(cached, group.requests)
        }

        // Generate new audio with optimal settings
        const audio = await this.studioIntegration.synthesizeWithEmotion(
          group.combinedText,
          group.voiceId,
          group.emotion,
          this.optimizeForCost(group.style)
        )

        await this.audioCache.set(cacheKey, audio, group.config)
        return this.splitAudioResponses(audio, group.requests)
      })
    )

    return results.flat()
  }

  // Real-time streaming with quality adaptation
  async streamAudioGeneration(
    text: string,
    config: StreamingConfig,
    onChunk: (chunk: AudioChunk) => void,
    onComplete: (fullAudio: AudioBuffer) => void
  ): Promise<void> {
    const stream = await this.studioIntegration.createStreamingSynthesis({
      text,
      voice_id: config.voiceId,
      chunk_length_schedule: [120, 160, 250, 500], // Progressive chunking
      streaming_latency: config.latencyMode || 'balanced'
    })

    let fullAudioBuffer: AudioBuffer[] = []
    let qualityMetrics: QualityMetric[] = []

    stream.on('chunk', (chunk: AudioChunk) => {
      // Monitor quality in real-time
      const quality = this.qualityMonitor.analyzeChunk(chunk)
      qualityMetrics.push(quality)

      // Adaptive quality adjustment
      if (quality.score < config.minQuality) {
        stream.adjustQuality({
          stability: Math.min(quality.stability + 0.1, 1.0),
          clarity: Math.min(quality.clarity + 0.1, 1.0)
        })
      }

      fullAudioBuffer.push(chunk.audio)
      onChunk(chunk)
    })

    stream.on('complete', () => {
      const fullAudio = this.combineAudioChunks(fullAudioBuffer)
      const finalQuality = this.qualityMonitor.analyzeFull(fullAudio)

      // Log quality metrics for optimization
      this.logQualityMetrics(finalQuality, qualityMetrics)

      onComplete(fullAudio)
    })
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Luma Ray3: Advanced Reasoning Video Generation

Luma Ray3 represents a paradigm shift in AI video generation by introducing reasoning capabilities that go beyond simple prompt-to-video conversion. Unlike traditional video generation models that rely primarily on pattern matching, Ray3 incorporates logical reasoning, temporal consistency, and contextual understanding to create videos that respond intelligently to complex scenarios.

### Understanding Ray3's Reasoning Architecture

Ray3's breakthrough lies in its multi-stage reasoning process that combines visual understanding, logical inference, and temporal modeling:

\`\`\`typescript
// Luma Ray3 integration with advanced reasoning capabilities
import { LumaAPI, VideoProject, ReasoningEngine } from '@lumalabs/ray3-sdk'

interface Ray3Configuration {
  reasoning: {
    contextualUnderstanding: boolean
    temporalConsistency: number
    logicalInference: boolean
    sceneComposition: SceneCompositionSettings
  }
  generation: {
    resolution: VideoResolution
    frameRate: number
    duration: number
    style: VideoStyle
    qualityProfile: QualityProfile
  }
  optimization: {
    renderingPipeline: RenderingPipeline
    memoryManagement: MemorySettings
    distributedProcessing: boolean
    cacheStrategy: CacheStrategy
  }
}

class LumaRay3Integration {
  private lumaAPI: LumaAPI
  private reasoningEngine: ReasoningEngine
  private videoProcessor: VideoProcessor
  private qualityOptimizer: QualityOptimizer

  constructor(config: Ray3Configuration) {
    this.lumaAPI = new LumaAPI({
      apiKey: process.env.LUMA_API_KEY,
      reasoning: config.reasoning,
      generation: config.generation
    })

    this.setupReasoningEngine(config)
    this.initializeVideoProcessing(config.optimization)
  }

  // Advanced prompt engineering for reasoning-based generation
  async generateReasoningVideo(
    scenario: VideoScenario,
    reasoningParameters: ReasoningParameters
  ): Promise<VideoGeneration> {
    // Phase 1: Contextual Analysis
    const contextAnalysis = await this.analyzeScenarioContext(scenario)

    // Phase 2: Logical Reasoning Chain
    const reasoningChain = await this.buildReasoningChain(
      scenario,
      contextAnalysis,
      reasoningParameters
    )

    // Phase 3: Video Generation with Reasoning Guidance
    const generation = await this.lumaAPI.generate({
      prompt: this.constructReasoningPrompt(scenario, reasoningChain),
      reasoning_chain: reasoningChain,
      temporal_guidance: {
        consistency_weight: 0.8,
        logical_flow: true,
        scene_transitions: reasoningChain.transitions,
        narrative_structure: reasoningChain.narrative
      },
      generation_settings: {
        resolution: '1920x1080',
        fps: 30,
        duration: scenario.duration,
        style: scenario.style,
        quality: 'cinematic'
      }
    })

    // Phase 4: Post-processing with reasoning validation
    const validatedVideo = await this.validateReasoningConsistency(
      generation.video,
      reasoningChain
    )

    return {
      video: validatedVideo,
      reasoningChain,
      qualityMetrics: generation.quality_metrics,
      processingTime: generation.processing_time
    }
  }

  // Complex scene understanding and logical inference
  private async buildReasoningChain(
    scenario: VideoScenario,
    context: ContextAnalysis,
    parameters: ReasoningParameters
  ): Promise<ReasoningChain> {
    const reasoningSteps: ReasoningStep[] = []

    // Analyze scenario components
    const characters = this.extractCharacters(scenario)
    const environment = this.analyzeEnvironment(scenario)
    const actions = this.identifyActions(scenario)
    const causality = this.buildCausalityGraph(actions)

    // Build logical reasoning chain
    for (const action of actions) {
      const step: ReasoningStep = {
        action: action.description,
        preconditions: this.identifyPreconditions(action, context),
        consequences: this.predictConsequences(action, causality),
        visual_elements: this.mapToVisualElements(action),
        temporal_constraints: this.calculateTemporalConstraints(action),
        logical_consistency: this.validateLogicalConsistency(action, reasoningSteps)
      }

      reasoningSteps.push(step)
    }

    // Validate overall chain consistency
    const chainValidation = await this.validateChainConsistency(reasoningSteps)

    return {
      steps: reasoningSteps,
      narrative_arc: this.constructNarrativeArc(reasoningSteps),
      visual_continuity: this.ensureVisualContinuity(reasoningSteps),
      logical_validation: chainValidation,
      temporal_structure: this.buildTemporalStructure(reasoningSteps)
    }
  }

  // Advanced video composition with reasoning-guided editing
  async composeReasoningVideo(
    segments: VideoSegment[],
    composition: VideoComposition
  ): Promise<ComposedVideo> {
    const reasoningGuidedComposition = await this.lumaAPI.compose({
      segments: segments.map(segment => ({
        video_data: segment.data,
        reasoning_context: segment.reasoningContext,
        temporal_position: segment.temporalPosition,
        transition_logic: segment.transitionLogic
      })),
      composition_reasoning: {
        narrative_flow: composition.narrativeFlow,
        visual_coherence: composition.visualCoherence,
        emotional_arc: composition.emotionalArc,
        logical_progression: composition.logicalProgression
      },
      editing_parameters: {
        cut_timing: 'reasoning_guided',
        transition_style: 'contextual',
        pacing_control: 'narrative_driven',
        continuity_enforcement: true
      }
    })

    return {
      composedVideo: reasoningGuidedComposition.video,
      editingDecisions: reasoningGuidedComposition.editing_log,
      qualityAnalysis: reasoningGuidedComposition.quality_analysis,
      reasoningValidation: reasoningGuidedComposition.reasoning_validation
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

### Production Video Processing Pipeline

Implementing Luma Ray3 in production requires sophisticated pipeline management to handle the computational complexity of reasoning-based video generation:

\`\`\`typescript
// Production-ready Ray3 video processing system
export class ProductionVideoSystem {
  private ray3Integration: LumaRay3Integration
  private processingQueue: VideoProcessingQueue
  private distributedRenderer: DistributedRenderingSystem
  private qualityAssurance: VideoQualityAssurance

  constructor() {
    this.setupProductionPipeline()
  }

  // Scalable video generation with intelligent resource management
  async processVideoRequest(request: VideoRequest): Promise<VideoResponse> {
    // Analyze computational requirements
    const complexity = await this.analyzeComplexity(request.scenario)
    const resources = this.allocateResources(complexity)

    // Queue management with priority scheduling
    const job = await this.processingQueue.enqueue({
      id: request.id,
      priority: this.calculatePriority(request),
      resources: resources,
      estimatedTime: this.estimateProcessingTime(complexity),
      request: request
    })

    // Distributed processing for complex scenarios
    if (complexity.requiresDistribution) {
      return this.processDistributed(job)
    }

    // Standard processing for simpler scenarios
    return this.processSingle(job)
  }

  // Intelligent quality assurance system
  private async validateVideoQuality(
    video: GeneratedVideo,
    originalRequest: VideoRequest
  ): Promise<QualityValidation> {
    const validation = {
      visual_quality: await this.assessVisualQuality(video),
      reasoning_consistency: await this.validateReasoningConsistency(
        video,
        originalRequest.reasoningChain
      ),
      temporal_coherence: await this.checkTemporalCoherence(video),
      narrative_flow: await this.validateNarrativeFlow(video),
      technical_specs: await this.verifyTechnicalSpecs(video, originalRequest.specs)
    }

    // Automated quality improvement suggestions
    const improvements = await this.suggestImprovements(validation)

    return {
      ...validation,
      overall_score: this.calculateOverallScore(validation),
      improvements: improvements,
      approved: this.determineApproval(validation)
    }
  }

  // Advanced caching and optimization
  private setupIntelligentCaching(): void {
    this.cache = new VideoCache({
      strategy: 'semantic_similarity', // Cache based on content similarity
      storage: {
        hot: 'redis',      // Frequently accessed
        warm: 's3',        // Occasionally accessed
        cold: 'glacier'    // Archive storage
      },
      compression: {
        algorithm: 'av1',  // Modern efficient compression
        quality_levels: ['draft', 'preview', 'production'],
        adaptive_bitrate: true
      },
      similarity_threshold: 0.85, // 85% similarity for cache hits
      invalidation: {
        time_based: 30 * 24 * 60 * 60, // 30 days
        usage_based: true,
        content_based: true
      }
    })
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Voice Assistant Development with Expo and ElevenLabs

The combination of Expo's cross-platform capabilities with ElevenLabs' advanced voice synthesis creates opportunities for building sophisticated voice assistants that work seamlessly across mobile, web, and desktop platforms. This integration enables natural conversational experiences with sub-200ms response times and contextual understanding.

### Cross-Platform Voice Assistant Architecture

Building production-ready voice assistants requires careful architecture to handle real-time audio processing, context management, and cross-platform compatibility:

\`\`\`typescript
// Advanced voice assistant with Expo and ElevenLabs integration
import { Audio } from 'expo-av'
import { ElevenLabsAPI } from '@elevenlabs/sdk'
import { SpeechRecognition } from '@react-native-voice/voice'

interface VoiceAssistantConfig {
  audio: {
    sampleRate: number
    channels: number
    bitDepth: number
    bufferSize: number
    latencyMode: 'low' | 'balanced' | 'high_quality'
  }
  speech: {
    recognition: SpeechRecognitionConfig
    synthesis: VoiceSynthesisConfig
    processing: AudioProcessingConfig
  }
  conversation: {
    contextWindow: number
    memoryManagement: MemoryConfig
    intentRecognition: IntentConfig
    responseGeneration: ResponseConfig
  }
}

class AdvancedVoiceAssistant {
  private elevenLabs: ElevenLabsAPI
  private audioRecorder: ExpoAudioRecorder
  private speechRecognition: SpeechRecognition
  private conversationManager: ConversationManager
  private contextEngine: ContextEngine

  constructor(config: VoiceAssistantConfig) {
    this.initializeAudioSystems(config)
    this.setupConversationEngine(config)
    this.configureRealTimeProcessing(config)
  }

  // Real-time conversation with context awareness
  async startConversation(
    initialContext?: ConversationContext
  ): Promise<ConversationSession> {
    const session = await this.conversationManager.createSession({
      context: initialContext,
      settings: {
        realTimeProcessing: true,
        contextualMemory: true,
        emotionalAwareness: true,
        multimodalInputs: true
      }
    })

    // Set up real-time audio pipeline
    await this.setupAudioPipeline(session)

    // Initialize conversation state
    await this.initializeConversationState(session)

    return session
  }

  // Advanced audio processing pipeline
  private async setupAudioPipeline(session: ConversationSession): Promise<void> {
    // Configure low-latency audio recording
    await this.audioRecorder.configure({
      android: {
        extension: '.wav',
        outputFormat: Audio.RECORDING_OPTIONS_PRESET_HIGH_QUALITY.android.outputFormat,
        audioEncoder: Audio.RECORDING_OPTIONS_PRESET_HIGH_QUALITY.android.audioEncoder,
        sampleRate: 44100,
        numberOfChannels: 1,
        bitRate: 128000,
      },
      ios: {
        extension: '.wav',
        outputFormat: Audio.RECORDING_OPTIONS_PRESET_HIGH_QUALITY.ios.outputFormat,
        audioQuality: Audio.RECORDING_OPTIONS_PRESET_HIGH_QUALITY.ios.audioQuality,
        sampleRate: 44100,
        numberOfChannels: 1,
        bitRate: 128000,
        linearPCMBitDepth: 16,
        linearPCMIsBigEndian: false,
        linearPCMIsFloat: false,
      },
    })

    // Set up real-time speech recognition
    this.speechRecognition.onSpeechStart = () => {
      session.handleSpeechStart()
    }

    this.speechRecognition.onSpeechPartialResults = (event) => {
      session.handlePartialSpeech(event.value[0])
    }

    this.speechRecognition.onSpeechResults = async (event) => {
      const transcript = event.value[0]
      await this.processUserSpeech(transcript, session)
    }
  }

  // Intelligent conversation processing
  private async processUserSpeech(
    transcript: string,
    session: ConversationSession
  ): Promise<void> {
    // Update conversation context
    const updatedContext = await this.contextEngine.updateContext({
      userInput: transcript,
      sessionHistory: session.getHistory(),
      currentContext: session.getContext(),
      emotionalState: session.getEmotionalState()
    })

    // Intent recognition with contextual understanding
    const intent = await this.recognizeIntent(transcript, updatedContext)

    // Generate contextually appropriate response
    const response = await this.generateResponse(intent, updatedContext)

    // Synthesize speech with emotional expression
    const audioResponse = await this.synthesizeResponse(response, updatedContext)

    // Play response and update session
    await this.playAudioResponse(audioResponse)
    session.addExchange({
      userInput: transcript,
      intent: intent,
      response: response,
      context: updatedContext,
      timestamp: new Date()
    })
  }

  // Advanced response synthesis with emotional intelligence
  private async synthesizeResponse(
    response: ConversationResponse,
    context: ConversationContext
  ): Promise<AudioBuffer> {
    const emotionalState = this.analyzeEmotionalContext(context)

    const synthesisConfig = {
      text: response.text,
      voice_id: context.preferredVoice || 'default',
      model_id: 'eleven_multilingual_v2',
      voice_settings: {
        stability: this.calculateStability(emotionalState),
        similarity_boost: 0.8,
        style: this.mapEmotionToStyle(emotionalState),
        use_speaker_boost: true
      },
      pronunciation_dictionary_locators: context.pronunciationCustomizations,
      emotion_control: {
        happiness: emotionalState.happiness,
        sadness: emotionalState.sadness,
        anger: emotionalState.anger,
        surprise: emotionalState.surprise
      }
    }

    return await this.elevenLabs.textToSpeech(synthesisConfig)
  }

  // Cross-platform audio playback optimization
  private async playAudioResponse(audioBuffer: AudioBuffer): Promise<void> {
    const sound = new Audio.Sound()

    try {
      // Convert AudioBuffer to playable format
      const audioUri = await this.convertAudioBufferToUri(audioBuffer)

      // Configure playback for optimal latency
      await sound.loadAsync(
        { uri: audioUri },
        {
          shouldPlay: false,
          isLooping: false,
          volume: 1.0,
          rate: 1.0,
          shouldCorrectPitch: true,
          progressUpdateIntervalMillis: 100,
          androidImplementation: 'MediaPlayer'
        }
      )

      // Play with interrupt handling
      await sound.setOnPlaybackStatusUpdate((status) => {
        if (status.isLoaded && status.didJustFinish) {
          sound.unloadAsync()
        }
      })

      await sound.playAsync()
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Audio playback error:', error)
      // Fallback to text display
      this.displayTextFallback(response.text)
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

### Production Voice Assistant Implementation

Building voice assistants for production deployment requires robust error handling, performance optimization, and scalability considerations:

\`\`\`typescript
// Production-ready voice assistant system
export class ProductionVoiceAssistant extends AdvancedVoiceAssistant {
  private performanceMonitor: PerformanceMonitor
  private errorHandler: ErrorHandler
  private scalabilityManager: ScalabilityManager
  private securityManager: SecurityManager

  constructor(config: VoiceAssistantConfig) {
    super(config)
    this.setupProductionInfrastructure()
  }

  // Advanced error handling and recovery
  private setupErrorHandling(): void {
    this.errorHandler = new ErrorHandler({
      strategies: {
        network_failure: 'retry_with_backoff',
        audio_processing_error: 'fallback_to_text',
        speech_recognition_failure: 'request_repeat',
        synthesis_error: 'cached_response',
        context_corruption: 'reset_conversation'
      },
      recovery: {
        automatic: true,
        user_notification: true,
        error_reporting: true,
        graceful_degradation: true
      }
    })
  }

  // Performance optimization for real-time processing
  private optimizePerformance(): void {
    this.performanceMonitor = new PerformanceMonitor({
      metrics: [
        'speech_recognition_latency',
        'response_generation_time',
        'synthesis_latency',
        'total_response_time',
        'context_processing_time'
      ],
      targets: {
        total_response_time: 200, // 200ms target
        synthesis_latency: 100,   // 100ms synthesis
        recognition_latency: 50   // 50ms recognition
      },
      optimization: {
        adaptive_quality: true,
        resource_scaling: true,
        caching_strategy: 'intelligent',
        preprocessing: true
      }
    })
  }

  // Intelligent conversation state management
  private async manageConversationState(
    session: ConversationSession
  ): Promise<void> {
    // Compress conversation history for efficiency
    if (session.getHistory().length > 50) {
      const compressed = await this.compressConversationHistory(
        session.getHistory()
      )
      session.setCompressedHistory(compressed)
    }

    // Predict next user intents
    const predictedIntents = await this.predictNextIntents(session)
    session.setPredictedIntents(predictedIntents)

    // Preload likely responses
    await this.preloadResponses(predictedIntents, session.getContext())
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Cross-Platform Implementation Strategies

Modern audio/video AI applications must work seamlessly across web, mobile, and desktop platforms. This requires careful architectural planning to handle platform-specific capabilities while maintaining a unified user experience.

### Unified Media Processing Architecture

Creating a cross-platform media processing system requires abstraction layers that handle platform differences while providing consistent APIs:

\`\`\`typescript
// Cross-platform media processing architecture
interface PlatformMediaCapabilities {
  audio: {
    recording: boolean
    playback: boolean
    realTimeProcessing: boolean
    backgroundProcessing: boolean
    hardwareAcceleration: boolean
  }
  video: {
    generation: boolean
    playback: boolean
    streaming: boolean
    hardwareDecoding: boolean
    webGL: boolean
  }
  ai: {
    onDeviceInference: boolean
    cloudProcessing: boolean
    edgeComputing: boolean
    gpuAcceleration: boolean
  }
}

class CrossPlatformMediaSystem {
  private platformCapabilities: PlatformMediaCapabilities
  private audioProcessor: UnifiedAudioProcessor
  private videoProcessor: UnifiedVideoProcessor
  private aiProcessor: UnifiedAIProcessor

  constructor() {
    this.detectPlatformCapabilities()
    this.initializeProcessors()
  }

  // Platform capability detection and adaptation
  private detectPlatformCapabilities(): void {
    const isWeb = typeof window !== 'undefined'
    const isReactNative = typeof navigator !== 'undefined' && navigator.product === 'ReactNative'
    const isElectron = typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.process?.type === 'renderer'

    this.platformCapabilities = {
      audio: {
        recording: this.checkAudioRecording(),
        playback: this.checkAudioPlayback(),
        realTimeProcessing: this.checkRealTimeAudio(),
        backgroundProcessing: !isWeb || isElectron,
        hardwareAcceleration: this.checkAudioHardwareAcceleration()
      },
      video: {
        generation: this.checkVideoGeneration(),
        playback: true, // Generally supported everywhere
        streaming: this.checkVideoStreaming(),
        hardwareDecoding: this.checkHardwareDecoding(),
        webGL: this.checkWebGL()
      },
      ai: {
        onDeviceInference: this.checkOnDeviceAI(),
        cloudProcessing: this.checkNetworkConnectivity(),
        edgeComputing: this.checkEdgeSupport(),
        gpuAcceleration: this.checkGPUAcceleration()
      }
    }
  }

  // Adaptive processing based on platform capabilities
  async processMediaRequest(
    request: MediaRequest,
    options: ProcessingOptions = {}
  ): Promise<MediaResponse> {
    // Determine optimal processing strategy
    const strategy = this.selectProcessingStrategy(request, this.platformCapabilities)

    // Platform-specific optimizations
    const optimizedRequest = await this.optimizeForPlatform(request, strategy)

    // Route to appropriate processor
    switch (request.type) {
      case 'audio':
        return this.audioProcessor.process(optimizedRequest, strategy)
      case 'video':
        return this.videoProcessor.process(optimizedRequest, strategy)
      case 'multimodal':
        return this.processMultimodal(optimizedRequest, strategy)
      default:
        throw new Error(\`Unsupported media type: \${request.type}\`)
    }
  }

  // Intelligent processing strategy selection
  private selectProcessingStrategy(
    request: MediaRequest,
    capabilities: PlatformMediaCapabilities
  ): ProcessingStrategy {
    const strategies: ProcessingStrategy = {
      location: 'cloud', // Default to cloud processing
      quality: 'high',   // Default to high quality
      latency: 'balanced',
      caching: true,
      fallback: []
    }

    // Optimize for mobile devices
    if (this.isMobileDevice()) {
      strategies.quality = request.priority === 'performance' ? 'medium' : 'high'
      strategies.caching = true
      strategies.fallback.push('reduce_quality', 'cloud_fallback')
    }

    // Optimize for real-time applications
    if (request.realTime) {
      strategies.location = capabilities.ai.onDeviceInference ? 'device' : 'edge'
      strategies.latency = 'low'
      strategies.quality = 'medium'
      strategies.fallback.push('reduce_latency')
    }

    // Optimize for offline scenarios
    if (!capabilities.ai.cloudProcessing) {
      strategies.location = 'device'
      strategies.fallback.push('cached_response', 'simplified_processing')
    }

    return strategies
  }
}
\`\`\`

### Platform-Specific Implementations

Each platform requires specific optimizations and implementations to take advantage of unique capabilities:

\`\`\`typescript
// Platform-specific implementations
class WebPlatformImplementation extends CrossPlatformMediaSystem {
  private webWorkers: Worker[] = []
  private webAssembly: WebAssemblyModule
  private webGL: WebGLRenderingContext

  constructor() {
    super()
    this.setupWebOptimizations()
  }

  // Web-specific optimizations
  private async setupWebOptimizations(): Promise<void> {
    // Load WebAssembly for intensive processing
    this.webAssembly = await this.loadWASMModule('/audio-processing.wasm')

    // Set up Web Workers for background processing
    this.webWorkers = await this.createWorkerPool(4)

    // Initialize WebGL for GPU acceleration
    this.webGL = this.setupWebGL()

    // Set up service worker for offline capabilities
    await this.setupServiceWorker()
  }

  // Web Worker-based processing
  async processAudioInWorker(audioData: AudioBuffer): Promise<ProcessedAudio> {
    const worker = this.getAvailableWorker()

    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      worker.postMessage({
        type: 'process_audio',
        data: audioData,
        timestamp: Date.now()
      })

      worker.onmessage = (event) => {
        if (event.data.type === 'audio_processed') {
          resolve(event.data.result)
        }
      }

      worker.onerror = reject
    })
  }
}

class ReactNativeImplementation extends CrossPlatformMediaSystem {
  private nativeModules: NativeModules
  private backgroundTasks: BackgroundTaskManager

  constructor() {
    super()
    this.setupNativeOptimizations()
  }

  // React Native-specific optimizations
  private setupNativeOptimizations(): void {
    // Access native audio processing modules
    this.nativeModules = require('react-native').NativeModules

    // Set up background task handling
    this.backgroundTasks = new BackgroundTaskManager()

    // Configure native audio session
    this.configureAudioSession()
  }

  // Native module integration
  async processWithNativeModule(
    data: MediaData,
    processingType: string
  ): Promise<ProcessedMedia> {
    const { AudioProcessingModule } = this.nativeModules

    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      AudioProcessingModule.processMedia(
        data,
        processingType,
        (error: Error, result: ProcessedMedia) => {
          if (error) {
            reject(error)
          } else {
            resolve(result)
          }
        }
      )
    })
  }
}

class ElectronImplementation extends CrossPlatformMediaSystem {
  private mainProcess: MainProcessBridge
  private nativeAcceleration: NativeAcceleration

  constructor() {
    super()
    this.setupElectronOptimizations()
  }

  // Electron-specific optimizations
  private setupElectronOptimizations(): void {
    // Bridge to main process for intensive operations
    this.mainProcess = new MainProcessBridge()

    // Access native acceleration features
    this.nativeAcceleration = new NativeAcceleration()

    // Set up file system access for caching
    this.setupFileSystemCaching()
  }

  // Main process delegation for intensive tasks
  async delegateToMainProcess(
    task: ProcessingTask
  ): Promise<ProcessingResult> {
    return this.mainProcess.execute({
      type: 'media_processing',
      task: task,
      options: {
        useNativeAcceleration: true,
        memoryLimit: '2GB',
        timeout: 300000 // 5 minutes
      }
    })
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Best Practices and Deployment

Deploying audio/video AI applications in production requires careful attention to performance, cost optimization, user experience, and scalability. Here are the essential best practices for successful deployment:

### Performance Optimization Strategies

\`\`\`typescript
// Comprehensive performance optimization system
class MediaAIPerformanceOptimizer {
  private metricsCollector: PerformanceMetrics
  private adaptiveQuality: AdaptiveQualitySystem
  private resourceManager: ResourceManager
  private cacheOptimizer: CacheOptimizer

  constructor() {
    this.setupPerformanceMonitoring()
  }

  // Intelligent quality adaptation based on device capabilities
  async optimizeForDevice(
    request: MediaRequest,
    deviceCapabilities: DeviceCapabilities
  ): Promise<OptimizedRequest> {
    const optimization = {
      quality: this.calculateOptimalQuality(deviceCapabilities),
      resolution: this.selectOptimalResolution(deviceCapabilities),
      bitrate: this.calculateOptimalBitrate(deviceCapabilities),
      processing: this.selectProcessingLevel(deviceCapabilities)
    }

    // Network-aware optimizations
    const networkQuality = await this.assessNetworkQuality()
    if (networkQuality.bandwidth < 1000000) { // Less than 1 Mbps
      optimization.quality = Math.min(optimization.quality, 0.7)
      optimization.resolution = this.reduceResolution(optimization.resolution)
    }

    // Battery-aware optimizations for mobile
    if (deviceCapabilities.isMobile && deviceCapabilities.batteryLevel < 0.2) {
      optimization.processing = 'low_power'
      optimization.quality = Math.min(optimization.quality, 0.5)
    }

    return this.applyOptimizations(request, optimization)
  }

  // Predictive resource allocation
  private async optimizeResourceAllocation(): Promise<void> {
    const usage_patterns = await this.analyzeUsagePatterns()
    const predicted_load = this.predictLoad(usage_patterns)

    // Pre-allocate resources based on predictions
    await this.resourceManager.preAllocate({
      cpu: predicted_load.cpu * 1.2, // 20% buffer
      memory: predicted_load.memory * 1.15, // 15% buffer
      gpu: predicted_load.gpu * 1.1, // 10% buffer
      network: predicted_load.network * 1.25 // 25% buffer
    })

    // Set up auto-scaling triggers
    this.resourceManager.setAutoScaling({
      scaleUp: { cpu: 80, memory: 85, gpu: 75 },
      scaleDown: { cpu: 40, memory: 50, gpu: 30 },
      cooldown: 300 // 5 minutes
    })
  }
}
\`\`\`

### Cost Optimization and Resource Management

\`\`\`typescript
// Advanced cost optimization system
class CostOptimizationEngine {
  private usageAnalyzer: UsageAnalyzer
  private pricingOptimizer: PricingOptimizer
  private resourceScheduler: ResourceScheduler

  constructor() {
    this.setupCostMonitoring()
  }

  // Intelligent request batching to reduce API costs
  async optimizeBatchProcessing(
    requests: MediaRequest[]
  ): Promise<BatchedRequests> {
    // Group similar requests for batch processing
    const batches = this.groupSimilarRequests(requests)

    // Optimize batch sizes based on pricing tiers
    const optimizedBatches = batches.map(batch => {
      const optimalSize = this.calculateOptimalBatchSize(
        batch.type,
        this.getCurrentPricing(batch.provider)
      )

      return this.splitBatch(batch, optimalSize)
    }).flat()

    // Schedule batches during off-peak pricing periods
    const scheduledBatches = await this.scheduleForOptimalPricing(optimizedBatches)

    return {
      batches: scheduledBatches,
      estimatedCost: this.calculateEstimatedCost(scheduledBatches),
      savingsPercentage: this.calculateSavings(requests, scheduledBatches)
    }
  }

  // Dynamic pricing strategy selection
  private selectOptimalProvider(
    request: MediaRequest,
    requirements: QualityRequirements
  ): ProviderSelection {
    const providers = this.getAvailableProviders(request.type)

    const evaluation = providers.map(provider => ({
      provider,
      cost: this.calculateCost(request, provider),
      quality: this.assessQuality(provider, requirements),
      latency: this.getAverageLatency(provider),
      reliability: this.getReliabilityScore(provider),
      score: this.calculateOverallScore(provider, request, requirements)
    }))

    // Select based on weighted criteria
    const optimal = evaluation.reduce((best, current) =>
      current.score > best.score ? current : best
    )

    return {
      primary: optimal.provider,
      fallback: this.selectFallbackProvider(evaluation, optimal),
      reasoning: this.explainSelection(optimal, evaluation)
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

### Production Deployment Architecture

\`\`\`typescript
// Production-ready deployment system
class ProductionDeploymentSystem {
  private infrastructure: InfrastructureManager
  private monitoring: MonitoringSystem
  private security: SecurityManager
  private scaling: AutoScalingSystem

  constructor() {
    this.setupProductionInfrastructure()
  }

  // Comprehensive deployment pipeline
  async deployToProduction(
    application: MediaAIApplication,
    environment: ProductionEnvironment
  ): Promise<DeploymentResult> {
    // Pre-deployment validation
    const validationResult = await this.validateDeployment(application)
    if (!validationResult.passed) {
      throw new DeploymentError('Validation failed', validationResult.errors)
    }

    // Infrastructure provisioning
    const infrastructure = await this.provisionInfrastructure(environment)

    // Database migrations and setup
    await this.setupDatabase(infrastructure.database)

    // Deploy application components
    const deployment = await this.deployComponents({
      api: application.api,
      frontend: application.frontend,
      workers: application.workers,
      infrastructure: infrastructure
    })

    // Configure monitoring and alerting
    await this.setupMonitoring(deployment)

    // Configure auto-scaling
    await this.configureAutoScaling(deployment, environment.scaling)

    // Run smoke tests
    const smokeTests = await this.runSmokeTests(deployment)
    if (!smokeTests.passed) {
      await this.rollbackDeployment(deployment)
      throw new DeploymentError('Smoke tests failed', smokeTests.errors)
    }

    return {
      deployment,
      infrastructure,
      monitoring: this.getMonitoringDashboard(deployment),
      healthCheck: this.getHealthCheckUrl(deployment)
    }
  }

  // Comprehensive monitoring setup
  private async setupMonitoring(deployment: Deployment): Promise<void> {
    await this.monitoring.configure({
      metrics: [
        'api_response_time',
        'audio_processing_latency',
        'video_generation_time',
        'error_rate',
        'throughput',
        'resource_utilization',
        'cost_per_request',
        'user_satisfaction_score'
      ],
      alerting: {
        response_time: { threshold: 500, severity: 'warning' },
        error_rate: { threshold: 5, severity: 'critical' },
        resource_usage: { threshold: 85, severity: 'warning' },
        cost_anomaly: { threshold: 50, severity: 'warning' }
      },
      dashboards: [
        'system_health',
        'performance_metrics',
        'cost_analysis',
        'user_experience'
      ]
    })
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Conclusion

The audio/video AI landscape has evolved into a sophisticated ecosystem of interconnected tools and technologies that enable unprecedented creative possibilities. ElevenLabs Studio 3.0's advanced audio synthesis capabilities, combined with Luma Ray3's reasoning-powered video generation, represent a new era where AI doesn't just process media—it understands context, maintains consistency, and creates with intention.

The integration of voice assistants through platforms like Expo with ElevenLabs demonstrates how these technologies can be seamlessly embedded into cross-platform applications, creating natural, conversational experiences that feel genuinely interactive. Meanwhile, tools like Nano Banana for AI image generation provide the foundational building blocks for comprehensive media processing pipelines.

Key developments that make 2024 a watershed moment for audio/video AI include real-time processing capabilities that enable sub-200ms response times, reasoning systems that understand context and maintain narrative consistency, cross-platform deployment strategies that work seamlessly across web, mobile, and desktop environments, and production-ready optimization techniques that balance quality, cost, and performance.

The architectural patterns and implementation strategies outlined in this guide provide a foundation for building scalable, performant audio/video AI applications. From intelligent caching systems that reduce costs and improve response times to adaptive quality systems that optimize for device capabilities and network conditions, these approaches enable developers to create production-ready applications that leverage the full power of modern AI media processing.

As these technologies continue to evolve, the convergence of audio, video, and AI processing will enable entirely new categories of applications—from immersive storytelling platforms that adapt to user preferences to intelligent content creation tools that understand brand guidelines and audience context. The patterns established today will form the foundation for the next generation of AI-powered media experiences.

The production deployment considerations covered here—from performance optimization and cost management to security and scalability—ensure that applications built with these tools can operate reliably at scale while providing consistent, high-quality user experiences across diverse platforms and network conditions.`,
